      "section": "When to get help",
      "text": "Get urgent advice (NHS 111 in England; local urgent care elsewhere) if the pain or swelling gets worse, you cannot put weight on the injury, or there are signs of infection. See a GP if it is not improving with self-care. Go to an emergency department if you heard a crack, the injured part looks deformed, it has gone numb, or the skin has changed colour, because a bone may be broken.",
